/F2 11 Tf 56 800 Td 14 TL
/F2 18 Tf (Heredity: inheritance and variation) Tj 0 -30 Td
/F2 14 Tf (Genes, chromosomes and DNA) Tj 0 -22 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Traits are characteristics that are passed from parents to their offspring, such as the) Tj T*
(shape of a seed or the colour of a flower. The instructions for traits are carried by genes.) Tj T*
(A gene is a segment of DNA, and genes are found on chromosomes inside the nucleus of a cell.) Tj T*
T*
(Human body cells contain 46 chromosomes arranged in 23 pairs. One chromosome of each pair) Tj T*
(comes from the mother and the other comes from the father. Because chromosomes come in) Tj T*
(pairs, most genes come in pairs too.) Tj T*
T*
(Different versions of the same gene are called alleles. For example, a gene for stem length) Tj T*
(in pea plants has one allele for tall stems and another allele for short stems.) Tj T*
T*
ET
endstream
