/F2 11 Tf 56 800 Td 14 TL
/F2 14 Tf (Patterns beyond simple dominance) Tj 0 -22 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Not every trait follows simple dominance. In incomplete dominance, the heterozygous) Tj T*
(offspring shows a phenotype in between the two parents. When a red-flowered four o'clock) Tj T*
(plant is crossed with a white-flowered one, the offspring have pink flowers.) Tj T*
T*
(In codominance, both alleles are fully expressed. Roan cattle have both red hairs and white) Tj T*
(hairs. In human ABO blood types, the A and B alleles are codominant, so a person who) Tj T*
(inherits both has type AB blood.) Tj T*
T*
(Some genes have more than two alleles in a population. The ABO blood type gene has three) Tj T*
(alleles: IA, IB and i. The i allele is recessive, so a person with type O blood has the) Tj T*
(genotype ii.) Tj T*
T*
(Sex-linked traits are controlled by genes on the X chromosome. Red-green colour blindness is) Tj T*
(more common in males because males have only one X chromosome, so a single recessive allele) Tj T*
(on that X chromosome is enough for the trait to appear.) Tj T*
T*
ET
